      "id": "curcan",
      "end": 1599,
      "contributors": [],
      "provenance": "Pleiades",
      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\"><em>C\u00fcrc\u0101n</em>: It is a famous city. It was built by\u00a0<em>C\u00fcrc\u0101n bin \u00dcmeym bin B\u016br\u0101n bin S\u0101m\u00a0bin N\u016b\u1e25 \u2018aleyhi\u2019s-sel\u0101m</em>. It is in the province of <em data-start=\"158\" data-end=\"168\">Khorasan</em>, to the west of <em data-start=\"185\" data-end=\"191\">Nes\u0101</em>.\u00a0Altogether,\u00a0there is another well-known city<span>\u00a0between\u00a0<em>\u1e6caberist\u0101n</em>\u00a0and\u00a0<em>Khwarazm</em>, rich in rainfall and with a good-flowing</span>\u00a0river. It is the <em data-start=\"323\" data-end=\"331\">C\u00fcrc\u0101n</em>\u00a0built in 98 (of the Hijri calendar) by <em data-start=\"389\" data-end=\"412\">Yaz\u012bd ibn al-Muhallab</em>. It was the first city founded in the province of <em data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"487\">M\u0101zender\u0101n</em>. Besides these two, there is another <em data-start=\"529\" data-end=\"537\">C\u00fcrc\u0101n</em> in the province of <em data-start=\"557\" data-end=\"567\">Khwarazm</em>. In <em data-start=\"572\" data-end=\"590\">Taqw\u012bm al-buld\u0101n</em>, all three are recorded. [translation]</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
      "description": "",
      "transcriptionCompleteness": "complete",
      "language": "ota",
